# Project Design Phase

## Project Title
Script-Controlled ACL – Restrict Record Access Based on Field Value

## System Design
The system uses a Script-Controlled Access Control List (ACL) in ServiceNow to control access to records based on a specific field value.

## Design Components
- ServiceNow Table
- Target Record
- Field Value
- Script-Controlled ACL
- User Access Validation
- Access Permission

## Working Flow
1. User requests access to a record.
2. The ACL checks the specified field value.
3. The script validates whether the user satisfies the required condition.
4. If the condition is satisfied, access is granted.
5. If the condition is not satisfied, access is denied.

## ACL Design
The ACL will contain a server-side script that checks the required field value and returns true or false based on the access condition.

## Expected Result
The designed system ensures that records are accessible only to users who satisfy the specified field-based access condition.
